      "text": [
        " مَا أَخَذَتِ الْحَبَائِلُ فَقَطَعَتْ مِنْهُ شَيْئاً فَهُوَ مَيِّتٌ وَ مَا أَدْرَكْتَ مِنْ سَائِرِ جَسَدِهِ فَذَكِّهِ ثُمَّ كُلْ مِنْهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Aban, from Zurara, ",
          "Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> has said: ‘What the snares seize, so something is cut off from it, so it is dead, and what you come to from the rest of its body, so purify (slaughter) it, then eat from it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Aban has narrated from Zurarah who has said the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Whatever of a prey is caught in the snare and is cutoff, it is dead, but what you find alive of the rest of the body, you can slaughter it properly and use it for food.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
